      <h2>The Sides: Texas Toast Griddle Sear &amp; Fry Dynamics</h2>
      <p>The accompanying sides elevate this meal above ordinary fast-food combos:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Texas Toast Maillard Sear:</strong> Thick-sliced Pullman white bread slathered in garlic butter and pressed on a 375°F flat-top griddle until crisp mahogany edges form. The interior remains pillowy and soft. Many diners tear the toast in half to build mini open-faced tender sandwiches.</li>
        <li><strong>The French Fry Protocol:</strong> The thin-cut shoestring fries are seasoned with fine salt. Because carryout steam softens fries rapidly, always request <em>"extra well-done fries"</em> at the order speaker to guarantee crispness through your drive home.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Sauced Baskets: Honey BBQ vs. Wild Buffalo</h2>
      <p>For diners who prefer pre-sauced heat, Dairy Queen offers two distinct flavor profiles:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Honey BBQ:</strong> A dark molasses and honey glaze that clings tightly to the breading ridges, caramelizing into a sweet, smoky bark.</li>
        <li><strong>Wild Buffalo:</strong> A bright, cayenne-forward vinegar sauce with moderate heat. We recommend requesting a side of DQ house ranch to balance the acidity.</li>
      </ul>

